  "goodToKnow": "Das Kriegsverbrechen is a war crime. The Nürnberger Prozesse (Nuremberg trials, 1945–46) tried leading Nazis and shaped modern international criminal law, now applied by the International Criminal Court in The Hague. Under the principle of universal jurisdiction, German courts can prosecute war crimes committed abroad; in 2022 a Koblenz court convicted a Syrian officer for crimes against humanity. Plural: die Kriegsverbrechen."
